2004: On December 26 a very strong earthquake on the western coast of the Aceh province north of Sumatra caused a tsunami that struck 14 countries, killing 226,000 people along the coast of the Indian Ocean.
2005: A series of strong earthquakes struck the west coast of Sumatra in late March and the beginning of April.
